      "message": "Separate CL, we can replace this (and any other instances) with `std::ranges::copy(p-\u003euserid, global_context.user_id.begin());`.\n\n**Why this is better:**\n\n* **Type Safety:** `memcpy` and `memcmp` operate on `void*` and bypass C++ type checking. `std::ranges` algorithms are type-aware.\n* **Bounds Checking:** By relying on ranges, the compiler determines the size of `global_context.user_id` and `p-\u003euserid` directly from their types, entirely eliminating the risk of `sizeof()` mismatches or buffer overflows.",
